  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Eswatini is increasingly experiencing the adverse impacts of several climate hazards. These hazards include increasing temperatures, shifting rainfall patterns and an increase in the frequency, intensity and duration of extreme weather events such as droughts and floods. A primary adverse impact is the decreased availability of water, which poses a significant threat to the country&#x2019;s water security. Reduced water availability has cascading negative repercussions on Eswatini&#x2019;s economy, affecting</narrative>
  </description>
